mme by UNESCO is related to which of the following?</span></p>","option_1":"Biosphere Reserve","option_2":"Ozone conservation","option_3":"National Clean Air Programme","option_4":"Nuclear waste","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Biosphere Reserve.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The Man and Biosphere (MAB) Programme is an Intergovernmental Scientific Programme launched by UNESCO in 1971 that aims to establish a scientific basis for improving relationships between people and their environments through the designation of Biosphere Reserves.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30930","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"826","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following fairs is NOT associated with Uttarakhand?</span></p>","option_1":"Thal Fair","option_2":"Pushkar Fair","option_3":"Jauljibi Fair","option_4":"Syalde Bikhauti Fair","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Pushkar Fair.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Pushkar Fair is held in Pushkar, Rajasthan, not Uttarakhand. Thal Fair, Jauljibi Fair, and Syalde Bikhauti Fair are all traditional fairs held in Uttarakhand.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30931","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"826","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Where did Maharaja Ranjit Singh establish his capital after reuniting the Sikh territories?</span></p>","option_1":"Lahore","option_2":"Amritsar","option_3":"Delhi","option_4":"Patiala","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Lahore.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Maharaja Ranjit Singh established Lahore as his capital after unifying the Sikh territories (misls) into a single Sikh Empire in 1799, ruling from there until his death in 1839.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30932","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"826","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>'Purnagiri Mela' is celebrated in which Indian state?</span></p>","option_1":"Assam","option_2":"Gujarat","option_3":"West Bengal","option_4":"Uttarakhand","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"4","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option D - Uttarakhand.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Purnagiri Mela is a religious fair held at the Purnagiri Temple in the Champawat district of Uttarakhand, dedicated to Goddess Purnagiri, attracting large numbers of pilgrims especially during Chaitra Navratri.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficult