e:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - 0.1.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>For a distinct echo to be heard, the reflected sound must reach the ear at least 0.1 seconds after the original sound, as the human ear can only distinguish two sounds as separate if there is a minimum gap of 0.1 seconds (persistence of hearing).</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30937","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"826","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>What component of a hearing aid receives sound?</span></p>","option_1":"Microphone","option_2":"Amplifier","option_3":"Speaker","option_4":"Battery","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Microphone.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>A hearing aid consists of a microphone (receives/picks up sound), an amplifier (increases the sound signal), a speaker/receiver (delivers amplified sound to the ear), and a battery (powers the device). The microphone is the component that receives sound.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30938","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"826","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Paradip Port is situated in the _______ delta.</span></p>","option_1":"Ganga","option_2":"Kaveri","option_3":"Mahanadi","option_4":"Luni","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Mahanadi.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Paradip Port, located in Odisha, is situated at the mouth of the Mahanadi River delta on the Bay of Bengal, and is one of India's major ports handling bulk cargo such as iron ore and coal.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30939","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"826","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following is NOT another name of the currency issued by the central bank of India?</span></p>","option_1":"High powered money","option_2":"Reserved money","option_3":"Line of credit","option_4":"Monetary base","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"3","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option C - Line of credit.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The currency issued by the Reserve Bank of India (the central bank) is also known as High Powered Money, Reserve Money, or Monetary Base — these terms refer to the same monetary aggregate (M0). \"Line of credit\" is a banking/lending term referring to a flexible loan facility, not another name for currency.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30940","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"826","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>\"This crop is grown in that season which begins with the onset of winter in October-November and ends in March-April.\"</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Which of the following crop can be grown in season given in the lines above?</span></p>","option_1":"Mustard","option_2":"Rice","option_3":"Cucumber","option_4":"Watermelon","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Mustard.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The season described (starting October-November, ending March-April) is the Rabi season. Mustard is a classic Rabi crop, sown in October-November and harvested in March-April. Rice, Cucumber, and Watermelon are Kharif/Zaid crops.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"30941","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"826","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Who is the author of the poetry collection 'Apocalypso'?</span></p>","option_1":"Jayant Kaikini","option_2":"Jeet Thayil","option_3":"Manjul Bajaj","option_4":"<style> @font-f